1
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:06,000
The death of Mona Dearly wasn't so much a whodunnit, as a who didn't.

2
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:06,000
Drowning Mona is a comedy, crime, mystery film directed by Nick Gomez.

3
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:06,000
The recently deceased Mona Dearly was many things: an abusive wife, a
domineering mother, a loud-mouthed neighbor and a violent malcontent.

4
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
So when her car and corpse are discovered in the Hudson River, police Chief
Wyatt Rash immediately suspects murder rather than an accident.

5
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
But, since the whole community of Verplanck, N.Y., shares a deep hatred for this unceasingly
spiteful woman, Rash finds his murder investigation overwhelmed with potential suspects.

6
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Chief Wyatt Rash, played by Danny DeVito.

7
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
Mona Dearly, played by Bette Midler.

8
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Ellen Rash, played by Neve Campbell.

9
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
Rona Mace, played by Jamie Lee Curtis.

10
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Bobby Calzone, played by Casey Affleck.

11
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
Phil Dearly, played by William Fichtner.

12
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
Drowning Mona is a 2000 American crime comedy film starring Danny DeVito as Wyatt Rash, a local police chief from Verplanck, New York, who investigates the mysterious death of Mona
Dearly (Bette Midler), a spiteful, hard-drinking, loud-mouthed, abusive woman, hated by all who knew her, who drove her son's car off a cliff and drowned in a river.

13
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
The film received negative reviews from critics.

14
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
The film explores themes of investigation, suspicion, remake, murder, death.

15
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
The tone is lighthearted and dark and thought_provoking.
